        "Machine learning, or ML, means training a model on past data so that it can predict something about new data. A plant wants to predict which curing presses will fail next week. A retailer wants to forecast how many tyres of each size each store will sell. Doing this well takes several steps: preparing features (the input columns the model learns from), training, tracking experiments, registering the chosen model, serving it so apps can ask for predictions, and watching it once it is live.",
